      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I do not completely get the second part, most avatars are actually using DXT type, since it is pretty much the default setting in unity, except one changes it willingly (with setting compression quality to high for example) to something like BC7. In case you are talking about crunch compression, it does nothing for vram size, only DL size. (see Unitys Documentation -> \"Crunch compression helps the texture use the lowest possible amount of disk space, but has no effect on runtime memory usage.\"\nThe issue is mainly, that people tend to use abnourmus sizes for textures, which are unecessary most of the time, so an option ingame to enforce lower texture resolutions would be very nice. (See https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/texture-size-limit-as-a-setting )",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-07-29T00:39:14.126Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As someone with 3GB of vram, when a lobby has more than 10-15 people in it, I have to make my exit without the ability to cut down on texture quality. Since this ability was taken away from me, I'm mostly unable to join public lobbies. Could we get some form of texture decimation for avatars? As a secondary request, I'd like DXT to be enforced in the SDK, I see too many avatars that demand 300mb of vram each and that's just crazy to me. Enforcing compression would also help quest users. Thanks for reading!",
